      "name": "DecompressTileData",
      "signature": "void DecompressTileData(int pTileData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Decompresses compressed tile data and initializes texture cache.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate cache index from pTileData[4] is non-negative (0x1eb)\n  2. If cache index != 0, use fast path via FUN_6f8a9530\n  3. Initialize 0x100 (256) DWORD buffer at DAT_6f8b9328 to zero\n  4. Decode tile data pairs: (count_byte, data_byte) format\n     - 0x00, 0x00 = end-of-row (move to next 32-byte row)\n     - count_byte > 0 = advance position by count_byte (0x1 per pixel)\n     - data_byte > 0 = copy data_byte bytes from input stream\n  5. Allocate cache entry via FUN_6f8a9420, get new cache index\n  6. Validate returned index (0x1f8, 0x1f9)\n  7. Lock texture memory surface (0x98 offset in vtable)\n  8. Copy decompressed data to texture surface via FUN_6f8a3390\n  9. Unlock texture memory surface (0x80 offset)\n  10. Update cache entry and release texture handle\n\nParameters:\n  pTileData (ECX) - Pointer to TileComp structure with compressed data\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates cache and texture resources\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Cache index 0: full decompression path (handles single texture)\n  - Cache index != 0: fast path reuses existing cache entry\n  - Requires 0x88 (136) bytes stack space for buffers\n  - Calls FogAssert on validation failures (3 assert points)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:8f35024d33e9f2523644111e730a06de",
