      "name": "SetRenderingQualityMode",
      "signature": "void SetRenderingQualityMode(int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets the rendering quality mode for the display device.\n\nAlgorithm\n  1. Check if requested mode (nMode) differs from current mode (g_dwCurrentRenderingMode)\n  2. If same mode is already active, return early (optimization)\n  3. Switch on mode value (1-4) to configure rendering parameters\n  4. For each mode, dispatch 3 display device function calls with mode-specific parameters\n  5. Update global current mode state (g_dwCurrentRenderingMode = nMode)\n  6. Return to caller\n\nParameters\n  ECX: nMode - Rendering quality mode (1=Low, 2=Medium, 3=High, 4=Maximum)\n\nReturns\n  None (void)\n\nSpecial Cases\n  - Redundant mode calls are optimized away (early return if mode unchanged)\n  - Invalid modes (0 or > 4) fall through to default case without state update\n  - Display device object (g_pDisplayDevice) must be initialized before calling\n  - Each mode configures 3 render parameters via function pointer dispatch",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7b88fe0bad13992be2100453c36d1589",
