      "name": "SetAlphaBlendMode",
      "signature": "void SetAlphaBlendMode(int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets the alpha blending mode for the display device.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load current alpha blend mode from g_dwAlphaInitialized\n  2. If uninitialized (0) or mode differs from current:\n     a. If nMode == 1: enable blend modes 0x10 (ADD) and 0x11 (MULTIPLY)\n     b. If nMode == 2: enable blend modes 0x10 (ADD) and 0x11 (MULTIPLY)\n  3. If nMode is neither 1 nor 2: do nothing (maintain current state)\n  4. Store mode in g_dwAlphaInitialized\n\nParameters:\n  nMode (ECX): Alpha blend mode (1 or 2)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call initializes alpha blending\n  - Redundant calls with same mode are skipped\n  - Invalid modes (not 1 or 2) are silently ignored",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c45575d9fb61a06993ec36c144d922f4",
