      "name": "CopySurfaceData",
      "signature": "void CopySurfaceData(void * pSrcSurface, void * pDstSurface)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies pixel data from source surface to destination surface\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Initialize two surface descriptor arrays (0x7c bytes each)\n  2. Call source surface Lock method (offset 0x64) to acquire pixel data\n  3. Call destination surface Lock method (offset 0x64) to acquire target buffer\n  4. Copy pixels in 32-bit chunks, then remaining 1-3 bytes individually\n  5. Advance source pointer by source pitch, destination by dest pitch\n  6. Repeat for each scanline (row) in surface\n  7. Call Unlock method (offset 0x80) on both surfaces\n  \n  Parameters:\n  pSrcSurface (ECX) - Pointer to source surface object with vtable\n  pDstSurface (EDX) - Pointer to destination surface object with vtable\n  \n  Returns:\n  void - Unlocks both surfaces and returns to caller\n  \n  Special Cases:\n  If source surface Lock fails, prints \"Failed to lock source surface\" error\n  If destination surface Lock fails, prints \"Failed to lock dest surface\" error\n  Copy loop is guarded by row count check; early exit if row count is 0\n  \n  Structure Layout - Surface Descriptor (0x7c bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n  0x00   | 4    | dwSize | dword | Descriptor size (0x7c)\n  0x34   | 4    | dwWidth | dword | Width in pixels\n  0x48   | 4    | pData | void* | Pointer to pixel data\n  0x50   | 4    | dwPitch | dword | Row pitch in bytes\n  0xB0   | 4    | dwHeight | dword | Height in scanlines",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:2cd9445b7edcfe613806f866bac9ebb1",
