      "name": "LogDirectDrawError",
      "signature": "undefined LogDirectDrawError(undefined4 pContext, int hResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Logs DirectDraw API error codes to the message queue with descriptive strings.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n  1. Receives HRESULT error code in param_2 (EDX, __fastcall)\\n  2. Uses binary search tree structure via CMP cascades to categorize error codes\\n  3. Maps error code to string pointer from lookup tables\\n  4. Calls QueueLogMessage with format string and error code\\n  5. Returns after logging (void return, no error handling)\\n\\nParameters:\\n  ECX (pContext): Context pointer (preserved in ESI, unused in function body)\\n  EDX (hResult): HRESULT error code from DirectDraw/Direct3D\\n    - Negative values (0x80000000+): Standard COM error codes\\n    - Examples: 0x80004001 (E_NOTIMPL), 0x80007057 (E_INVALIDARG)\\n    - DirectDraw errors: 0x8876XXXX (DDERR_*) range\\n    - Zero value (D3D_OK) also logged as error\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void (no return value)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Handles 150+ specific DirectDraw/Direct3D HRESULT codes\\n  - Uses jump tables at 0x6f8a4c4c, 0x6f8a4c68, 0x6f8a4cbc, 0x6f8a4d58, etc.\\n  - Unmapped error codes fall through to default case (0x6f8a4bef)\\n  - All paths call QueueLogMessage(0x6f8b4d48, pContext, hResult, pStringPtr)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
