      "name": "ReleaseCachedObjects",
      "signature": "void ReleaseCachedObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Release and clear all cached COM objects from two global object arrays.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Initialize ESI=0 (array offset), EDI=0 (NULL compare value)\n    2. Start loop to process 0x180 bytes (96 elements, 4 bytes each)\n    3. Load pointer from g_aCachedObjectsArray1 at offset ESI\n    4. If pointer is non-NULL, call virtual Release() method at vtable+0x8\n    5. Clear pointer to NULL after Release\n    6. Load pointer from g_aCachedObjectsArray2 at same offset\n    7. If pointer is non-NULL, call virtual Release() method at vtable+0x8\n    8. Clear pointer to NULL after Release\n    9. Increment offset by 4 bytes (next array element)\n    10. Repeat until offset reaches 0x180 bytes, then return\n\n  Parameters:\n    (none)\n\n  Returns:\n    void (always succeeds, no error return values)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
