      "name": "BlitBinkVideoFrame",
      "signature": "void BlitBinkVideoFrame(dword nClipX1, dword nClipY1, dword nClipX2, dword nClipY2, byte bPaletteIndex, int nBlendMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders a Bink video frame to the display device with clipping and blend mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Clamp clip X1 to range [0, dwMaxWidth-1]\n  2. Clamp clip X2 to range [0, dwMaxWidth-1]\n  3. Ensure X1 <= X2, otherwise skip rendering\n  4. Clamp clip Y1 to range [0, dwMaxHeight-1]\n  5. Clamp clip Y2 to range [0, dwMaxHeight-1]\n  6. Ensure Y1 <= Y2, otherwise trigger assertion\n  7. Setup Bink rendering state and device blend mode\n  8. Initialize 4 corner vertex structures with texture coordinates (0.5, 0.5) to (1.0, 1.0)\n  9. Get palette color and apply alpha blend mode bits (0x40/0x80/0xc0/0xff)\n  10. Call device DrawPrimitive to render clipped frame quad\n\nParameters:\n  nClipX1     - Left edge clip coordinate\n  nClipY1     - Top edge clip coordinate\n  nClipX2     - Right edge clip coordinate\n  nClipY2     - Bottom edge clip coordinate\n  bPaletteIndex - Palette color index (0-255)\n  nBlendMode  - Alpha blend mode: 0=0x40000000, 1=0x80000000, 2=0xc0000000, other=0xff000000\n\nReturns:\n  void (renders quad to display device via COM interface)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:d6b2f0f72f65614949b3186205c56b3d",
