      "name": "RenderBinkFrame",
      "signature": "void RenderBinkFrame(int nX1, int nY1, int nX2, int nY2, uint dwPaletteIndex, byte bAlpha)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders a Bink video frame within a rectangular region using Direct3D\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Validate rectangle bounds against Bink width/height tables\n  2. Get palette color for given index via GetPaletteColor\n  3. Setup Bink rendering state via SetupBinkState(2)\n  4. Set rendering quality mode based on alpha value\n  5. Apply alpha blending if bAlpha != 0xff (0x1c4 = point list format)\n  6. Render single vertex if rectangle is degenerate (point)\n  7. Render two-vertex strip for normal rectangle\n  \n  Parameters:\n  nX1 (ECX) - Left/starting X coordinate\n  nY1 (EDX) - Top/starting Y coordinate\n  nX2 - Right/ending X coordinate\n  nY2 - Bottom/ending Y coordinate\n  dwPaletteIndex - Palette color index (0-255)\n  bAlpha - Alpha/transparency value (0xff = opaque, 0x00 = transparent)\n  \n  Returns: None\n  \n  Special Cases:\n  - Bounds checking: Uses g_dwBinkWidthTable and g_dwBinkHeightTable limits\n  - Point rendering: When (nX1==nX2 && nY1==nY2), renders single vertex\n  - Alpha handling: 0xff uses quality mode 1, other values use mode 4 with alpha shift\n  - RHW values: Fixed 0x3f800000 (1.0 in IEEE float) for homogeneous coordinates\n  - U/V coordinates: Fixed 0x3f000000 and 0x3f800000 (0.5 and 1.0 in texture space)\n  \n  Structure Layout (Vertex Format):\n  Offset|Size|Field|Type|Description\n  0x00|4|fX|float|X coordinate\n  0x04|4|fY|float|Y coordinate  \n  0x08|4|dwZ|uint|Z coordinate/depth\n  0x0c|4|dwRHW|uint|Reciprocal homogeneous W (1.0)\n  0x10|4|dwColor|uint|ARGB color with alpha\n  0x14|4|dwSpecular|uint|Specular (unused, 0)\n  0x18|4|fU|float|Texture U coordinate\n  0x1c|4|fV|float|Texture V coordinate",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:34330d3891083c21fe25a080d9341bdf",
