      "name": "InitializeRenderSurface",
      "signature": "void InitializeRenderSurface(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the render surface with bink video dimensions or clears it based on transparency mask.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Load transparency mask flag (offset 0x28 from gdwBitMasks_exref)\n  2. If transparency flag set (TEST result != 0):\n     - Call ClearRenderSurface and exit\n  3. Otherwise load bink video dimensions (height, width)\n  4. Call texture COM object virtual method at offset 0x50:\n     - Parameter 1: g_pTextureCOM (this pointer)\n     - Parameter 2: 1 (count)\n     - Parameter 3: &dwZero2 (pointer to zero value)\n     - Parameter 4: 1 (blend or render mode)\n     - Parameter 5: 0xff000000 (black color ARGB)\n     - Parameters 6-7: 0 (unused)\n  \n  Returns: void\n  \n  Special Cases:\n  - Transparency mask determines whether surface is cleared or initialized\n  - Bink video dimensions are loaded as DWORD values\n  - Direct virtual method invocation through g_pTextureCOM\n  \n  Globals:\n  - g_dwTransparencyMask: Transparency flag mask (offset 0x28)\n  - g_dwBinkHeightTable: Bink video height\n  - g_dwBinkWidthTable: Bink video width\n  - g_pTextureCOM: COM texture object pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
