      "name": "AllocateFloorCacheEntry",
      "signature": "short AllocateFloorCacheEntry(FloorCacheManager * pCache)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Moves a free node to the allocated list and updates cache indices.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If allocated count matches capacity (nActiveCount == dwHeadValue), swap out:\n     a. Get node from free list head (pFreeHead)\n     b. If node exists: update links, set prev to 0\n     c. If first allocation: set pAllocatedHead = node\n     d. Else: insert after pAllocatedTail in doubly-linked list\n     e. Increment nActiveCount\n  2. Loop while nActiveCount < capacity:\n     a. Dequeue from allocated list head (pAllocatedHead)\n     b. Clear prev/next pointers and field at offset +0x4\n     c. Enqueue to free list (pFreeHead/pFreeTail)\n     d. Decrement nActiveCount\n     e. Allocate new node from free list\n     f. Repeat step 1a-e\n  3. Return when nActiveCount == capacity OR node value != 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nParameters:\n  pCache (ECX) - Pointer to FloorCacheManager structure:\n    Offset  | Field         | Type     | Description\n    --------|---------------|----------|--------------------------------------------\n    +0x0    | dwHeadValue   | uint     | Sentinel value (typically 0xFFFFFFFF)\n    +0x4    | nActiveCount  | uint     | Current active allocation count\n    +0x8    | pAllocatedHead| node*    | First allocated node (doubly-linked)\n    +0xC    | pAllocatedTail| node*    | Last allocated node (doubly-linked)\n    +0x10   | pFreeHead     | node*    | First free node (doubly-linked)\n    +0x14   | pFreeTail     | node*    | Last free node (doubly-linked)\n\nReturns:\n  Index (1-based) of allocated node (pAllocatedTail->field[0])\n  Return path: nActiveCount incremented, node linked into allocated list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First allocation: pAllocatedHead set to new node\n  - Subsequent allocations: node inserted after pAllocatedTail\n  - Free list exhaustion: eviction loop dequeues oldest allocations\n  - Sentinel check: continues until node->dwValue != 0xFFFFFFFF",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
