      "name": "RemoveListNode",
      "signature": "void RemoveListNode(ListControl * pListHead, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a doubly-linked list and adds it to the free list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if list count is 0; exit if empty\n  2. Load head pointer from list control structure (offset 0x8)\n  3. Calculate node address: array_base + (index * 0x18)\n  4. If node is head of list:\n     - Update head pointer to node's next link\n     - Clear tail if head becomes NULL\n  5. Else if node is tail of list:\n     - Update tail pointer to node's prev link  \n     - Clear next pointer of new tail\n  6. Else node is in middle:\n     - Link prev node's next to current node's next\n     - Link next node's prev to current node's prev\n  7. If node has external reference (field at offset 0x4):\n     - Clear referenced memory at external_ptr + 0x42\n     - Clear external reference field\n  8. Add removed node to free list:\n     - If free list empty, initialize with this node\n     - Else append to end of existing free list\n  9. Decrement count field (offset 0x4)\n\nParameters:\n  pListHead: Pointer to ListControl structure containing:\n    +0x4 dwCount: Count of active list entries\n    +0x8 pHead: Head of active doubly-linked list\n    +0xc pTail: Tail of active doubly-linked list\n    +0x10 pFreeListHead: Head of free list\n    +0x14 pFreeListTail: Tail of free list\n    +0x18 pArrayBase: Base of array containing node pointers\n  nIndex: Array index of node to remove (multiplied by 0x18 for stride)\n\nReturns:\n  void (function modifies list structure in-place)\n  - Active list node is moved to free list\n  - Count is decremented\n  - All pointers updated to maintain list integrity",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:922fa81000968bfbfdc5a374220f77a5",
