      "name": "InitializeDirectoryBuffer",
      "signature": "void InitializeDirectoryBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the global directory data buffer for game objects.\nClears monster tracking globals and allocates a 64KB buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize all monster state tracking globals to 0xFFFFFFFF\n  2. Call FogMemAlloc to allocate 0x10000 (65536) bytes of memory\n  3. Store allocated buffer pointer in g_pDirectoryData global\n  4. Zero-fill entire buffer using REP STOSD (0x4000 DWORDs = 16384 entries)\n  5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT: None - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  IMPLICIT: None - void function returns via RET, no return value in EAX\n\nNotes:\n  Initializes critical directory tracking structure for game objects.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
