      "name": "ClearBinkSurfaces",
      "signature": "void ClearBinkSurfaces(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears Bink video playback surfaces by setting high bit in each pixel word.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Initialize 0x80-byte stack buffer for surface data\n    2. Process primary Bink surface (g_pBinkPrimarySurface):\n       a. Lock surface via vtable offset 0x64 (Lock method)\n       b. Write 0x4000 words (64 iterations \u00d7 256 words)\n       c. Each word has 0x8000 bit set (high bit marking valid/initialized)\n       d. Stride is 0x400 bytes per iteration\n       e. Unlock surface via vtable offset 0x80 (Unlock method)\n    3. Process back buffer surface (g_pBinkBackSurface) with identical pattern\n\n  Parameters:\n    None. Uses global Bink surface pointers.\n\n  Returns:\n    void. Logs errors via LogDirectDrawError if surface operations fail.\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - Calls LogDirectDrawError (0x6f8b3344 and 0x6f8b3308) for lock/unlock failures\n    - Processing two separate surfaces with 0x4000-word blocks\n    - High bit (0x8000) set in each pixel for surface buffer management",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:5fd0f2e64755bf126ef29d9055c34540",
