      "name": "InitColorPaletteMultiplyTable",
      "signature": "void InitColorPaletteMultiplyTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a 256x256 byte lookup table for fast color multiplication.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Iterate through 256 rows (outer loop, EBX = row index 0-255)\n  2. For each row, iterate through 256 columns (inner loop, ECX = column index 0-255)\n  3. Compute table[row][col] = (row * col) / 255 using optimized integer division\n  4. Division by 255 uses magic constant 0x80808081 for fast multiplication-based divide\n  5. Result is clamped to byte range [0, 255]\n\n  Table Layout:\n  - Base address: 0x6f8c3270 (g_aColorPaletteTable)\n  - Size: 0x10000 (65536) bytes = 256 rows x 256 columns\n  - End address: 0x6f8d3270\n  - Access pattern: table[row * 0x100 + col] or table[row][col]\n\n  Parameters:\n  None - this function takes no parameters\n\n  Returns:\n  void - modifies global g_aColorPaletteTable in place\n\n  Usage:\n  Used by RenderTilesToVertexBuffer for color palette transformations.\n  Multiplies source color component by alpha/intensity value efficiently:\n    result = g_aColorPaletteTable[alpha * 0x100 + colorComponent]\n  This is equivalent to: result = (alpha * colorComponent) / 255\n\n  Special Cases:\n  - Row 0: All values are 0 (0 * col / 255 = 0)\n  - Column 0: All values are 0 (row * 0 / 255 = 0)\n  - Diagonal (row == col): Values equal row (row * row / 255 \u2248 row for row < 16)\n  - Row 255, Col 255: Value is 255 (255 * 255 / 255 = 255)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:a38cbadbfa76c6a39202431100665e44",
