      "name": "SetPaletteValues",
      "signature": "void SetPaletteValues(byte byValue1, byte byValue2, byte byValue3)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Stores three palette color values into global variables\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load first parameter (byValue1) from stack via CL register\n  2. Store byValue1 to g_byPaletteValue1\n  3. Store byValue2 (passed in DL) to g_byPaletteValue2\n  4. Store byValue3 to g_byPaletteValue3\n\nParameters:\n  byValue1 (CL): First palette color value component\n  byValue2 (DL): Second palette color value component\n  byValue3 (AL): Third palette color value component\n\nReturns:\n  None. Sets global palette state variables as side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Used during palette initialization/setup. Function uses __fastcall convention\n  with parameters in CL, DL, and AL registers for efficient byte parameter passing.",
