      "name": "ProcessCachePool",
      "signature": "void ProcessCachePool(CachePool * pPool)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Rebalances a doubly-linked list cache pool by moving items between active and temporary lists\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. If nCount != nMaxItems, process temporary items: remove from active list,\n     clear forward/back pointers (offsets 0x18, 0x1c), and optionally clear\n     parent array reference (offsets 0x4, 0x8)\n  2. While temp items exist: move to appropriate list based on sorting order\n     (compare item[0] vs nMaxItems), adjust counts and pointers\n  3. After each item processed, check item[0] for -1 (end marker) to exit loop\n\nParameters:\n  pPool (ECX)  Pointer to CachePool structure\n    [0x0]  nMaxItems: Maximum item count threshold\n    [0x4]  nCount: Current active item count\n    [0x8]  pHead: Head of active list (forward link)\n    [0xc]  pTail: Tail of active list (back link)\n    [0x10] pFreeList: Head of free list (forward link)\n    [0x14] pFreeTail: Tail of free list (back link)\n    [0x18] pTemp: Head of temp list (forward link)\n    [0x1c] pTempTail: Tail of temp list (back link)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if nCount reaches nMaxItems without proper balance\n  - Calls FogAssert for invariant violations (assertion failure invokes FUN_6f8aaff9)\n  - Links are cleared at 0x18, 0x1c; parent refs at 0x4, 0x8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:3d4fadde66f69063c154715c65b0086a",
