      "name": "PlayBinkVideo",
      "signature": "void PlayBinkVideo(char * pszFilename, int nPlayMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Play a Bink video file with optional audio processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Log playback start event\n  2. Check if Bink system already initialized via DAT_6f8b9310\n  3. Query expansion flag (0x4 for base, 0x5 for expansion)\n  4. Open file using SFileOpenFileEx with appropriate search scope\n  5. Encode playback mode into flags (0x800000 base, 0x30000000 for mode 1, 0x10000000 for mode 2, 0x40000000 for mode 3)\n  6. Open Bink file handle via _BinkOpen@8 with encoded flags\n  7. Calculate video dimensions: DAT_6f8b9308 = (DAT_6f8ba39c - *BinkHandle) >> 1, align to 4-byte boundary\n  8. Calculate video height: DAT_6f8b930c = (DAT_6f8ba658 - BinkHandle[1]) >> 1\n  9. Initialize frame loop with GetTickCount() baseline\n  10. Loop processing frames:\n     - Check abort conditions every 500ms: DAT_6f8b931c set, DAT_6f8baa9c set, or user action\n     - Process window messages (PeekMessageA, TranslateMessage, DispatchMessageA)\n     - When ready, call _BinkDoFrame@4 and lock surface via vtable method at offset 0x64\n     - Copy frame buffer via _BinkCopyToBuffer@28 to surface\n     - Unlock surface via vtable method at offset 0x80\n     - Advance frame via _BinkNextFrame@4 or set completion flag\n  11. Cleanup: SetSoundVolume(0), _BinkClose@4, CloseHandle, SetSoundVolume(0xff)\n\nParameters:\n  pszFilename (ECX) - Path to Bink video file to play\n  nPlayMode (EDX) - Video playback mode (0=silent, 1=mode1, 2=mode2, 3=mode3)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, function terminates on completion or abort\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Respects global abort flags: DAT_6f8b931c (stop signal), DAT_6f8baa9c (shutdown)\n  - User input handling: Mouse click (0x201), Escape key (0x102), keyboard (0x12), quit (0x204, 0x207)\n  - Supports callback injection via global callback pointer at [ESP+0xb8]\n  - Handles critical section locking for multithreaded surface access via DAT_6f8baaa0\n  - Frame skipping if Bink indicates frame wait = 0 but surface lock fails\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field              | Type    | Description\n  0x0    | 4    | nWidth             | uint    | Video width (calculated from offset table)\n  0x4    | 4    | nHeight            | uint    | Video height (calculated from offset table)\n  0x8    | 4    | nCurrentFrame      | uint    | Current frame index\n  0xc    | 4    | nTotalFrames       | uint    | Total frame count (completion when equals current)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
