      "name": "RenderTileFloorToSurface",
      "signature": "int RenderTileFloorToSurface(TileProject * pTile)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders a tile's floor graphics to a DirectDraw memory surface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Allocate tile project buffer via AllocateTileProjectBuffer\n  2. Validate cache index (sCacheIndex >= INVALID_HARDWARE_ADDRESS)\n  3. If cache index is 0 (uncached):\n     a. Allocate new cache entry from g_tFloorCache via FUN_6f8a6690\n     b. Store cache index at pTile+0x42 (1-based)\n     c. Calculate cache entry pointer: g_pFloorCacheEntries + (index-1) * 0x18\n     d. Lock DirectDraw surface via IDirectDrawSurface::Lock (vtable+0x64)\n     e. Verify DDSD_PITCH flag (0x8) is set in surface descriptor\n     f. Clear surface buffer (height * pitch bytes)\n     g. Iterate floor subtiles at pTile+0x54 (count at pTile+0x50)\n     h. For each subtile with flag 0x1 (visible):\n        - If flag 0x4 set: decode RLE-compressed data (15 rows)\n        - Else: decode diamond-shaped raw data (15 rows, 4-32-4 pattern)\n        - Convert 8-bit palette indices to 16-bit via g_awPaletteColorLUT\n     i. Unlock surface via IDirectDrawSurface::Unlock (vtable+0x80)\n     j. Blit to screen or copy via FUN_6f8a39e0\n  4. If already cached: promote entry in LRU list via FUN_6f8a67a0\n  5. Submit surface to display via interface at DAT_6f8baa94 (vtable+0x98)\n\nParameters:\n  pTile (ECX) - Pointer to TileProject structure containing:\n    +0x42: sCacheIndex - Cache slot (0=uncached, -1=invalid)\n    +0x50: nSubtileCount - Number of floor subtiles\n    +0x54: pSubtiles - Pointer to subtile array (0x14 bytes each)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE) if rendering succeeded\n  0 (FALSE) if AllocateTileProjectBuffer failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Cache index < 0: Assert failure (invalid hardware address)\n  - Cache index == 0: Full render path (allocate, lock, draw, unlock)\n  - Cache index > 0: Fast path (reuse cached surface, update LRU)\n  - Subtile flag 0x1: Visible subtile (must be set to render)\n  - Subtile flag 0x4: RLE-compressed format vs raw diamond format\n\nStructure Layout (Subtile at pSubtiles[i], 0x14 bytes each):\n  Offset | Size | Field    | Type   | Description\n  -------|------|----------|--------|---------------------------\n  0x00   | 2    | wX       | short  | X position in surface\n  0x02   | 2    | wY       | short  | Y position in surface\n  0x08   | 2    | wFlags   | ushort | Bit flags (0x1=visible, 0x4=RLE)\n  0x10   | 4    | pData    | byte*  | Pointer to pixel data",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:1e003ffbbcaf467825f8c7021a37f260",
