      "name": "ValidateVideoConfig",
      "signature": "int ValidateVideoConfig(void)",
      "calling_convention": "unknown",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates video configuration for Diablo II compatibility\n  \nAlgorithm:\n  1. Get fog state pointer; assert if NULL (abort at line 0xa9 if NULL)\n  2. Check version compatibility: if version=3 AND version_float < min_version, log warning and return 0\n  3. Load registry path from g_szVideoConfigPath string (22 bytes)\n  4. Query DeviceName registry value into local buffer\n  5. If DeviceName not found, return 0\n  6. Query dwFlags registry value into g_dwTransparencyMask\n  7. If dwFlags not found, return 0\n  8. If transparency mask conflicts with bitmask table, verify registry entry size (0x10 bytes)\n  9. If registry entry missing or wrong size, return 0\n  10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 if video config valid, 0 if invalid or assertion failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1de091de38a0c8104999bec46fd52d0f",
