      "name": "ShutdownBinkDirect3DRenderer",
      "signature": "void ShutdownBinkDirect3DRenderer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes Direct3D rendering window and releases all DirectDraw/Direct3D resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if Bink rendering is initialized (g_bBinkRenderInitialized)\n  2. Log \"Closing Direct3D window...\" message\n  3. Flush pending D3D operations (FUN_6f8a60c0)\n  4. Release DirectDraw surfaces (ReleaseDirectorySurfaces)\n  5. Clear tile/floor caches (either full clear or cache reset)\n  6. Release three DirectDraw surfaces (g_dw*SurfaceCache)\n  7. Clear rendering device references\n  8. Restore gamma ramps if support object exists (offset 0x10)\n  9. Release remaining COM objects by calling Release() vtable method (offset 0x08)\n  10. Log \"Direct3D window closed\" message\n  11. Clear initialization flag\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  void - function always succeeds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_bBinkRenderInitialized is 0, function returns immediately (already cleaned up)\n  - Gamma restoration error 0x887601c2 is silently ignored (already in invalid mode)\n  - All COM object pointers are set to NULL after Release() to prevent double-free\n  - g_pDDSurfaceDevice uses indirect pointer access (pointer to pointer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:cf3de18e3446e9b538dbe2c586a8037e",
