      "name": "InitializeTileCache",
      "signature": "int InitializeTileCache(dword * pCache, int nStartOffset, int nEndOffset, dword dwTileSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize a tile cache structure with surface/texture pairs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate tile count: (nEndOffset - nStartOffset) / dwTileSize, cap at 0x400 (1024)\n  2. Allocate buffer: count * 0x18 (24 bytes per tile), stores in pCache[6]\n  3. Zero-initialize allocated buffer using STOSD (dword) and STOSB (byte)\n  4. Initialize cache metadata fields in pCache structure:\n     - pCache[1-3]: set to 0 (head/tail pointers)\n     - pCache[4]: first element pointer (pCache[6])\n     - pCache[5]: last element pointer (pCache[6] + count*0x18 - 0x18)\n  5. For each tile slot, initialize linked list and create surface texture:\n     - offset 0x0: slot index\n     - offset 0x10: pointer to next slot (if not last)\n     - offset 0x14: pointer to previous slot (if not first)\n     - offset 0x8, 0xc: call CreateDeviceSurfaceTexture to set up surfaces\n  6. On texture creation failure, unlink failed slot and return current count\n  7. Return: nStartOffset + (final_count * dwTileSize)\n\nParameters:\n  pCache (ECX): pointer to cache control structure (24-byte header + dynamic tile array)\n  nStartOffset (EDX): starting offset/address for tile calculations\n  nEndOffset (Stack[0x4]): ending offset/address for tile calculations\n  dwTileSize (Stack[0x8]): size of each tile in bytes (used for return calculation)\n\nReturns:\n  On success: next available offset (nStartOffset + initialized_count * dwTileSize)\n  On allocation failure: terminates via FUN_6f8aaff9 (fatal error handler)\n  On texture creation failure: returns offset of failed slot\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If tile count exceeds 0x400, cap at 0x400 (1024 tiles maximum)\n  - Linked list uses doubly-linked structure with offsets within array\n  - Each tile is 0x18 (24) bytes: [index:4][next:4][prev:4][surface1:4][surface2:4][unused:4]\n  - Allocation failure triggers assertion and non-return function call\n  - Returns early if texture creation fails, leaving cache partially initialized",
