      "name": "ClearFloorCacheItems",
      "signature": "void ClearFloorCacheItems(dword * pCache, dword bFreeLinkedItems)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys/clears all items in the floor cache, optionally freeing linked item lists.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate input cache pointer (non-null)\n  2. Check cache consistency: if nNumItems == 0, verify item list is empty\n  3. Call destructor methods (vtable offset 0x8) on all cached items\n     at offsets +0x8 and +0xc within each cache entry (0x18 bytes apart)\n  4. Zero out the destructor pointers after calling destructors\n  5. If bFreeLinkedItems: walk linked list at cache[1] and free items to pool\n     Update linked list pointers (prev/next at +0x10, +0x14)\n     Clear item reference at offset +0x42 (2 bytes)\n  6. If pool data exists at cache[6], call ReleasePoolAllocation()\n  7. Zero cache[6] (clear pool reference)\n  8. Clear 7 DWORDs of cache structure state\n\nParameters:\n  pCache (ECX):  Pointer to cache structure with layout:\n    [0]=nMaxItems [1]=nNumItems [2]=first_item [3]=last_item\n    [4]=free_head [5]=free_tail [6]=pool_ptr [7..13]=reserved\n  bFreeLinkedItems (EDX):  If non-zero, free cached items via linked list\n\nReturns:\n  void (registers preserved per calling convention)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if pCache is NULL (calls FUN_6f8aaff9 with -1)\n  - Asserts if cache is empty but item count non-zero\n  - Safe to call multiple times (clearing already-cleared cache is no-op)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
