      "name": "PromoteFloorCacheEntry",
      "signature": "void PromoteFloorCacheEntry(int * pCache, int nItemIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Promotes a floor cache entry to the front of the doubly-linked list (MRU).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate cache has items (count > 1) and index is valid (1 <= nItemIndex <= count)\n2. Locate the cache node at the calculated offset: base + (nItemIndex - 1) * 0x18\n3. If node is the head, nothing to do; if empty list, initialize list with node\n4. Remove node from its current list position by updating prev/next pointers\n5. Insert node at the front (after head, before current head)\n6. Update cache head pointer to the promoted node\n\nParameters:\n  pCache (ECX): Pointer to cache structure with layout:\n    Offset | Field Description\n    -------|-------------------\n    +0x0   | Current item count\n    +0x4   | Max count validation\n    +0x8   | Head pointer (MRU item)\n    +0xc   | Tail pointer (LRU item)\n    +0x18  | Base address of pool\n  nItemIndex (EDX): 1-based index into cache pool (1 to count)\n\nReturns:\n  void (modifies cache in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if nItemIndex == 0 (invalid)\n  - Asserts if nItemIndex > count (out of bounds)\n  - Asserts if count > 1 (early exit if single item)\n  - Silent no-op if list empty (count == 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
