      "comment": "Processes a single frame of Bink video playback.\n\n  Algorithm\n    1. Check video type flag at pBinkState[1]\n      - If 'p' (0x70): Call FUN_6f8a7140 with fixed dimensions (0x1d4, 0x3c)\n      - If 's' (0x73): Process Smack/RAD video frame (main path)\n        a. Retrieve Smack handle from pBinkState[0]\n        b. Call SmackWait to check frame ready status\n        c. If SmackWait returns 0 (frame ready):\n          - Check if Bink rendering enabled via g_bBinkRenderEnabled\n          - Call SmackDoFrame to decode video frame\n          - Call FUN_6f8a73f0 for frame rendering setup\n          - Compare frame counters at offset 0x374 vs 0xc\n          - If counters match: Close video (SmackClose), clear pBinkState[0]\n          - If counters differ: Advance to next frame (SmackNextFrame)\n          - Check g_bGameShutdown flag\n          - Copy surface/texture data based on transparency mask\n        d. If SmackWait returns non-zero: Skip to parameter update\n        e. Call FUN_6f8a7140 with frame dimensions from pBinkState[4,8]\n\n  Parameters\n    pBinkState (ECX): Pointer to video state structure\n      - Offset 0x0: Smack handle (void*)\n      - Offset 0x4: Type flag ('p' or 's') + padding\n\n  Returns\n    void: No return value\n\n  Special Cases\n    - Video type 'p': Special playback mode with fixed resolution\n    - Video type 's': Normal Smack video rendering\n    - Shutdown check (g_bGameShutdown) can exit early\n    - Transparency mask (g_dwTransparencyMask) determines copy method",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
