      "name": "RenderBinkVideoQuads",
      "signature": "void RenderBinkVideoQuads(int * pBinkState, int nFrameWidth, int nVerticalOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders two textured quads for Bink video playback using Direct3D.\n\n  Algorithm\n    1. Retrieve video dimensions from pBinkState (offset 0x8=baseX, 0xc=height)\n    2. Configure rendering state:\n       - SetupBinkState(1): Set texture stage state for video\n       - SetRenderingQualityMode(1): Set point/bilinear filtering\n       - SetAlphaBlendMode(1): Enable alpha blending\n    3. Build first quad (left 256px strip):\n       - Populate 4 vertices in g_aBinkVertexBuffer (28 bytes each)\n       - Vertex format: D3DFVF_XYZRHW|D3DFVF_TEX1 (0x1c4)\n       - X coords: baseX to baseX+0x100 (256 pixels)\n       - Y coords: height-offset to height\n       - Texture U: 0.5 to 1.0, V: 0.5 to 1.0\n    4. Bind g_apBinkDeviceTextures via SetTexture (vtable+0x98)\n    5. Draw quad via DrawPrimitiveUP (vtable+0x70): D3DPT_TRIANGLEFAN, 4 verts\n    6. Build second quad (right strip based on frame width):\n       - X coords: baseX+0x100 to baseX+nFrameWidth\n       - Texture U scaled by g_fTexCoordScale (1/256 = 0.00390625)\n    7. Bind g_pBinkMemorySurfaceAlt texture\n    8. Draw second quad\n\n  Parameters\n    pBinkState (ECX)     Pointer to Bink video state structure\n      - Offset 0x8: Base X coordinate (int)\n      - Offset 0xc: Video height (int)\n    nFrameWidth (EDX)    Width of video frame in pixels\n    nVerticalOffset (Stack) Vertical offset for top edge positioning\n\n  Returns\n    void\n\n  Special Cases\n    - First quad is always 256 pixels wide (0x100)\n    - Second quad width varies based on nFrameWidth\n    - Magic values: 0x3f000000 = 0.5f, 0x3f800000 = 1.0f\n    - D3D constants: 6 = D3DPT_TRIANGLEFAN, 0x1c4 = D3DFVF_XYZRHW|D3DFVF_TEX1\n\n  Structure Layout (Vertex Buffer Entry - 28 bytes per vertex)\n    Offset  Size  Field    Type   Description\n    0x00    4     fX       float  Screen X coordinate\n    0x04    4     fY       float  Screen Y coordinate\n    0x08    4     fU       float  Texture U coordinate (0.5-1.0)\n    0x0c    4     fV       float  Texture V coordinate (0.5-1.0)\n    0x10    4     dwRHW    DWORD  Reciprocal homogeneous W (0 or 1.0)\n    0x14    4     dwColor  DWORD  Diffuse color (0x3f800000 = white)\n    0x18    4     dwSpec   DWORD  Specular color (0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
