      "name": "InitializeRenderingSurfaces",
      "signature": "void InitializeRenderingSurfaces(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes rendering surfaces and textures for the game engine\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify decompression buffer (sgpbDecompressionBuffer) is NULL, fail if not\n2. Verify highlight buffer (sgpbHighlightBuffer) is NULL, fail if not\n3. Allocate 0x10000 (65536) bytes for decompression buffer\n4. Allocate 0x10000 (65536) bytes for highlight buffer\n5. Create 256x256 memory surface texture (0x100x0x100)\n6. Verify surface creation succeeded, fail if not\n7. Create 128x128 memory surface texture (0x80x0x80)\n8. Verify surface creation succeeded, fail if not\n9. Create 32x32 memory surface texture (0x20x0x20)\n10. Verify surface creation succeeded, fail if not\n11. Initialize Direct3D structure with pixel format and buffer properties\n   - dwWidth = 0x10 (16 bits per pixel)\n   - dwCaps = 0x10800 (DDSCAPS_VIDEOMEMORY | DDSCAPS_PRIMARYSURFACE)\n   - dwHeight = 0x1c4 (452 - buffer stride/pitch)\n   - dwPaletteFormat = 0x30 (DDPF_PALETTEINDEXED8)\n12. Call Direct3D device method at offset +0x24 to finalize surface setup\n13. If setup fails, call HandleDirect3DError and return\n14. Initialize celfile callback and return\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fails immediately if buffers already allocated (prevents double allocation)\n  - Terminates with FUN_6f8aaff9(-1) on any assertion failure\n  - Direct3D device must be valid (g_pD3DDevice)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
