      "name": "CleanupRendererResources",
      "signature": "void CleanupRendererResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup renderer resources and release all Direct3D object references.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Release primary renderer object (0x6f8c3264) by calling virtual destructor at offset +0x8\n  2. Release vertex buffer pool (0x6f8c325c) handle via ReleasePoolAllocation(0x84)\n  3. Release index buffer pool (0x6f8c3260) handle via ReleasePoolAllocation(0x8a)\n  4. Loop through 3 texture/state block pairs (ESI += 0x4, count=0xc):\n     - Release texture from g_aTextureArray + ESI by calling virtual destructor at offset +0x8\n     - Release state block from g_aStateBlockArray + ESI by calling virtual destructor at offset +0x8\n  5. Clear all pointers to NULL after cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  (none)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer checks performed before calling destructors\n  - Array size hardcoded to 3 elements (0xc bytes / 4 bytes per pointer)\n  - Uses virtual method dispatch (vtable offset +0x8) for polymorphic cleanup\n  - Pool release sizes: 0x84 bytes (vertex), 0x8a bytes (index)",
