      "name": "RenderSkillGlyph",
      "signature": "dword RenderSkillGlyph(void * this, SkillGlyphInfo * pGlyph, dword dwColor)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Renders a skill glyph graphic to a surface cache, applying palette and color effects.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Validate skill object by checking vtable pointer (dereference this[0])\n  2. Call GetSkillData() to retrieve skill data structure\n  3. Normalize color parameter: if dwColor==0x4, convert to size 1 for reuse detection\n  4. Determine cache entry size based on glyph dimensions:\n     - If width < 0x20 && height < 0x20: size = 3\n     - Else if width < 0x80 && height < 0x80: size = 2\n     - Else if width < 0x100 && height < 0x100: size = 1\n     - Else: return 0 (too large)\n  5. Check if matching cache entry exists (same size, color parameter)\n  6. If not found or color mismatch:\n     - Allocate new cache entry\n     - Clear decompression buffer with zeros (0 to cbDataSize)\n     - Call D2CMP_DecodeAndDrawCelFrame() to decode CEL frame data\n     - Apply palette effects based on size: (1=standard, 2=palette lookup, 3=highlight)\n     - Call ConvertPalettedToRGB16() to convert to device format\n  7. Submit texture to Direct3D device via SetTexture()\n  8. Return success (1)\n\n  Parameters:\n  pGlyph (ECX): SkillGlyphInfo structure pointer:\n    offset +0x0: void* vtbl - virtual method table\n    offset +0x4: int nXPos - X position in pixels\n    offset +0x8: int nYPos - Y position in pixels\n    offset +0xC: int nXOffset - X offset for frame extraction\n    offset +0x10: int nXMin - bounding box left coordinate\n    offset +0x14: int nWidth - glyph width in pixels\n    offset +0x18: int nHeight - glyph height in pixels\n    offset +0x1C: uint cbDataSize - decompressed buffer size\n  dwColor (stack +4): dword color parameter (1-3, or 4=normalize to 1)\n\n  Returns:\n  EAX = 1 (success, always returns successfully)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
