      "name": "SetupBinkRenderQuad",
      "signature": "void SetupBinkRenderQuad(void * pVideoData, int nOffsetX, int nOffsetY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Prepares and renders a Bink video frame as a textured quadrilateral.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize Bink rendering state with SetupBinkState(1) and alpha blending\n  2. Extract video metadata from pVideoData structure (offsets 0x10-0x2c)\n  3. Apply zoom scaling to coordinates if g_dwZoomScale != 0x100\n  4. Calculate screen coordinates: X range [0x0-0x4], Y range [0x0-0x4]\n  5. Request renderer output buffer via g_pPrimaryRenderer[0xc](0x21)\n  6. On success, populate 4 vertices with X,Y texture coords, alpha=1.0\n  7. Perform indexed draw call: g_pD3DDevice[0x88](mode=6, count=4, stride=0x1c)\n  8. Increment g_dwCelfileCallbackInitialized, wrap at 0x2b\n\nParameters:\n  pVideoData [ECX] - Pointer to Bink video structure with layout:\n                     +0x0c = nLeft, +0x10 = nRight, +0x14 = nTop,\n                     +0x18 = nBottom, +0x20 = dwFlags, +0x24 = dwTexture,\n                     +0x28 = nPaletteIndex, +0x2c = dwBlendMode\n  nOffsetX [EDX]   - X coordinate offset applied to all vertices\n  nOffsetY [Stack] - Y coordinate offset applied to all vertices\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value, modifies renderer state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If GetBinkVideoInfoValue() == 0, skips zoom scaling\n  - If nPaletteIndex == 0 AND (nBottom+nOffsetY+nTop) == 0.0, calls FUN_6f8a9cc0\n  - Otherwise uses palette data from g_GameState[0x114][nPaletteIndex*3]\n  - Wraps g_dwCelfileCallbackInitialized at 0x2b (43 decimal)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:dec69381adff9469fa930bf868106105",
