      "name": "SetPaletteBlendedColor",
      "signature": "void SetPaletteBlendedColor(void * pObject, uint dwPaletteIndex, uchar byBlend)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Writes a palette-blended color value to object at offset 0x10.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Extract palette index low byte (0xFF mask) for palette table lookup\n  2. Scale index by shifting left 8 bits to calculate palette table offset\n  3. Sample three palette entries from color palette table:\n     - Entry 1: palette_table[g_byPaletteValue1 + (index << 8)]\n     - Entry 2: palette_table[g_byPaletteValue2 + (index << 8)]\n     - Entry 3: palette_table[g_byPaletteValue3 + (index << 8)]\n  4. Combine three bytes into 32-bit COLORREF format: 0xBBGGRR00\n  5. Write result to [pObject + 0x10]\n\nParameters:\n  ECX pObject - pointer to object to update (structure with color field at +0x10)\n  EDX dwPaletteIndex - palette color index (0-255), automatically masked to low byte\n  [ESP+0xC] byBlend - blend modifier used in palette table sampling\n\nReturns:\n  void - updates object in-place at offset 0x10\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Global palette value variables (g_byPaletteValue1, g_byPaletteValue2, g_byPaletteValue3)\n    control which palette entries are sampled from the palette table\n  - Result color is in COLORREF format: 0xBBGGRR00 (no alpha channel)\n  - Index parameter is automatically ANDed with 0xFF in EDX",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b6388a2a512d58984999da1e1e4b0f40",
