      "name": "SetColorFromPalette",
      "signature": "void SetColorFromPalette(D3DTLVERTEX * pVertex, dword dwColor, byte byAlpha)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the vertex color (ARGB) at offset 0x10 using palette lookup.\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Extract low byte of dwColor as palette index (bits 0-7)\n  2. Shift palette index left 0x8 (multiply by 0x100) to get row offset in table\n  3. Add base address 0x6f8c3270 to get base palette row (g_aColorPaletteTable)\n  4. Extract color component indices from dwColor and look up values in palette:\n     - bits 8-15 (blue): palette[palette_base + blue_index]\n     - bits 16-23 (green): palette[palette_base + green_index]\n     - bits 24-31 (red): palette[palette_base + red_index]\n  5. Pack result as ARGB dword: byAlpha | (blue << 8) | (green << 16) | (red << 24)\n  6. Write result to pVertex->color (offset 0x10)\n\n  Parameters:\n  pVertex (ECX): Pointer to D3DTLVERTEX structure, color written to offset 0x10\n  dwColor (EDX): Color value where bits [0:7]=palette_index, [8:15]=blue_idx, [16:23]=green_idx, [24:31]=red_idx\n  byAlpha (stack+0x10): Alpha channel (0-255), becomes low byte in result\n\n  Returns: void (result written to pVertex[0x10])\n\n  Special Cases:\n  - Uses global g_aColorPaletteTable at 0x6f8c3270 (256x256 byte lookup table)\n  - Each row is 0x100 (256) bytes for palette indices 0-255\n  - Palette lookup enables color remapping and transparency effects\n  - Result is Direct3D ARGB color format (A=MSB, R=LSB)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4ce3cb9d9d5cbb52ac0f0fc19ea60053",
