      "name": "RenderTileWall",
      "signature": "int RenderTileWall(int * pType, int nOffsetX, int nOffsetY, int * pColor, byte bShowTransparency, int nClipRect)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders a wall tile from a surface to the screen using 3D transformation and blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate surface type (0-9) against assertion\n  2. Calculate screen position bounds from clip rectangle (0x14 bytes)\n  3. For each surface entry in tile:\n     a. Extract offset index from surface header\n     b. Validate offset index (0-4) against assertion\n     c. Calculate base world coordinates from surface data tables\n     d. Transform 4 wall corner points to screen space\n     e. Perform frustum culling check against view rectangle\n  4. If visible:\n     a. Decompress tile data from surface memory\n     b. Calculate center world point and blend color between two palette colors\n     c. For each vertex row (8 rows total):\n        - Transform vertex center point to screen space\n        - Fill in adjacent wall edges with D3DTLVERTEX structures\n        - Apply palette color to all 4 vertices\n     d. Submit 4-triangle strip (0x1c4) to Direct3D device\n  5. Return success flag (1 if rendered, 0 if culled)\n\nParameters:\n  pType (ECX): Pointer to tile surface array, contains type in [0], references in [0x14-0x15]\n  nOffsetX (EDX): World X-axis offset (left-shifted 0xd places in register)\n  nOffsetY (EBX): World Y-axis offset (left-shifted 0xd places in register)\n  pColor: Palette color indices for blending (ARGB pairs at [0] and [4])\n  bShowTransparency: Transparency mode flag\n  nClipRect: Viewport clip rectangle (passed to CalculateWallClipRect)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX=1: Wall tile rendered successfully\n  EAX=0: Wall tile culled (outside viewport)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assertion failures on invalid surface type or offset index terminate with FUN_6f8aaff9(0xffffffff)\n  - Frustum culling prevents rendering outside viewport bounds\n  - Blends colors from two palette entries by averaging ARGB components\n  - Renders 4-vertex triangles with perspective-corrected D3D transformation\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Surface Entry Format (at [pType + 0x15]):\n    Offset | Size | Field            | Type   | Description\n    0x00   | 2    | nOffsetX_Packed  | short  | Bit 15-5: offset index, Bit 4-0: unused\n    0x02   | 2    | nResourceIndex   | ushort | Index into resource data table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
