      "name": "ParseDecimalString",
      "signature": "void ParseDecimalString(char * pDecimalString, int stringLength, uint * pFixedPointResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts decimal string to 96-bit fixed-point normalized representation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 3-dword output array to zero\n2. For each character in input string (stringLength iterations)\n   - Shift 96-bit mantissa left by 4 bits (multiply by 16)\n   - Load ASCII digit character and add to mantissa\n3. Begin normalization: if high_dword is zero, shift right by 16-bit chunks\n   - Each 16-bit right shift decrements exponent by 0x10\n4. Continue normalization: shift left until high bit of high_dword is set\n   - Each 1-bit left shift decrements exponent by 1\n5. Store final exponent at offset +0xa in output array\n\nParameters:\npDecimalString (char*): Pointer to decimal digit string to parse\nstringLength (int): Number of characters to process from string\npFixedPointResult (uint*): Pointer to 96-bit output array\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result stored in pFixedPointResult array at offsets 0x0, 0x4, 0x8 (mantissa), 0xa (exponent)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nEmpty string (stringLength=0) returns all zeros in output array\nInitial exponent 0x404e is adjusted during normalization\nStack canary protection XORs guard seed with frame pointer\nHigh bit test (0x8000) controls final normalization loop",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6dd9e098c401c5314529c240c6cfca58",
